# memory_gap_null_host_map: In-process, a range the host gives no memory (host address NULL) cannot be mapped: mach_vm_remap from address 0 plus the offset fails. A buffer over one of its pages faults its exec (the whole range in one piece), and so does a buffer over its last page and the first page of the range after it, which has memory (the first of two pieces fails); a task whose task root page is there faults its define. A buffer over the following range alone, and one in the first range, work. Map setup only: the blocks setup has no memory map, and in the isolate setup the first define faults (memory_gap_null_host_define).
